  "chapter_name": "",
  "level": 1,
  "question": "[Image] A → D is an endothermic reaction occurring in three (elementary) steps: (i) A → B, ΔHi = +ve; (ii) B → C, ΔHii = -ve; (iii) C → D, ΔHiii = -ve. Which of the following graphs between potential energy (y-axis) vs reaction coordinate (x-axis) correctly represents the reaction profile of A → D? Four candidate energy-profile plots (1)-(4) are shown in the source image, each with three peaks/steps but differing in the relative heights of the peaks and in whether the final product D ends up higher or lower than the initial reactant A. Refer to the source image for the exact curve shapes.",
